            "value": [
              {
                "dsDescriptionValue": {
                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "<p>Project UP Data Management Plan Quantitative Data</p>\n<p>Project UP aims to obtain knowledge on risk and protective mechanisms that play a role in unintended pregnancies. For data analyses, we will (re-)use readily available data from the Generation R cohort, a study of families in multi-ethnic Rotterdam. Specifically, we examine: Who is at risk for an unintended pregnancy, and how do risk factors cluster together? Which factors predict the non-use of contraceptives? What factors explain the link between unintended pregnancies and negative outcomes in children? What factors protect against the negative outcomes of unintended pregnancies?</p>"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
